From 43c05a59071ecc91142f6faa56c012fdf45b51d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hongchan Choi <hongchan@google.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:16:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Backport] CVE-2026-118358: Memory corruption in WebAudio

Cherry-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8561977:
Stop paused destination and guard automatic pull on close

When an AudioContext is closed while its frame is frozen, the platform
audio destination is in the kPaused state (`IsPlaying()` is false), so
`StopPlatformDestination()` previously skipped calling `Stop()`. When
the frame later thawed, `Resume()` restarted the audio thread on the
closed context, and `Render()` invoked `ProcessAutomaticPullNodes()`
even when pulling the audio graph was disabled, causing an object
lifetime issue with disposed upstream nodes.

Changes:
- Call `platform_destination_->Stop()` in `StopPlatformDestination()`
  whenever `platform_destination_` is present so `kPaused` destinations
  transition to `kStopped`.
- Move `ProcessAutomaticPullNodes()` inside the active graph-pulling
  branch of `RealtimeAudioDestinationHandler::Render()`.
- Add `AudioContextTest.CloseWhileFrozenStopsDestination` to verify
  closing a frozen context stops the destination and guards automatic
  pull nodes.

Bug: 572191610
Test: blink_unittests --gtest_filter=AudioContextTest.CloseWhileFrozen*
Change-Id: I3126957a0a43ffdce2f541908ad90359e8f0fd6e
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8561977
Commit-Queue: Hongchan Choi <hongchan@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Mahesh Kannan <kmaheshb@google.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717977}
Reviewed-on: https://codereview.qt-project.org/c/qt/qtwebengine-chromium/+/784488
Reviewed-by: Michal Klocek <michal.klocek@qt.io>
